\n#### Story 15: Remove credentials for a configured InvenioRDM instance\n- **Remove Action**: Configured instances display a \"Remove\" button.\n- **State Update**: Clicking \"Remove\" deletes the associated token from the internal session state (`configuredInstances` set).\n- **UI Feedback**: The view automatically refreshes to show the instance as \"Not Configured\", and a success notification is displayed.\n\n### Technical Details:\n- **Component Choice**: Switched from `TextField` to `PasswordField` for token input to follow security best practices.\n- **UI Pattern**: Used the project's existing `Section` and `Tag` components to maintain visual consistency.\n- **State**: Used a `java.util.Set<String>` to track configured instances within the prototype's scope.\n\nThe prototype can be tested by running the application with the `development` profile and navigating to `/test-view/associated-datasets-v2`."
